+// DevHub: the launcher this workbench's integrated terminal must run, or
+// undefined in a workbench nothing hosts.
+//
+// DevHub hosts this workbench, and its terminal is the tmux session DevHub
+// owns — not a shell the workbench chooses. It is per window, because a window
+// on a host must run the launcher written *there*, so DevHub names it on the
+// window configuration it opens the window with.
+//
+// From the *configuration*, not from `nodeProcess.env`. `preload.ts` does
+// `Object.assign(process.env, resolvedConfiguration.userEnv)`, but the
+// `process` a sandboxed renderer's preload sees materialises `env` from a
+// snapshot, so that assignment lands on a copy nothing reads back — every
+// window's `vscode.process.env['DEVHUB_TERMINAL']` was null while its
+// configuration held the right path. Nothing upstream noticed because nothing
+// upstream reads `userEnv` out of the renderer's environment. The window
+// configuration is the channel that actually carries a per-window fact, so it
+// is the only one DevHub uses.
